descriptionText:
As a Senior QA Engineer at Plus One Robotics, you will ensure that our robotic systems, including the software and hardware that make them up, are dependable and of the highest quality.&nbsp;


You will deploy and test software on Linux-based industrial PCs (IPCs), build and maintain automated test suites, analyze logs and stack traces to pinpoint failures, and verify that products work end to end in a physical robot cell. You will work closely with developers to find and verify fixes, with product owners to confirm the product does what they intended, and with customers to understand how it is used in the field.&nbsp;


This is a senior level position; we are not considering entry-level candidates for this role.&nbsp;


Essential Functions&nbsp;
Software Testing and Automation&nbsp;

- Define and implement testing strategies for new and existing products, covering functional, regression, integration, performance, and stability testing&nbsp;
- Create detailed, comprehensive, and well-structured test plans, test cases, and documentation from requirements, user stories, and acceptance criteria&nbsp;
- Develop and maintain automated test suites to validate functionality, performance, and stability. Integrate tests into CI/CD pipelines so builds are validated before release. Perform manual tests when automation isn't feasible
- Build internal tools and scripts to optimize and automate QA workflows, test data collection, and log analysis&nbsp;
Deployment, Debugging, and Defect Management&nbsp;

- Install, deploy, and configure software builds and deploy packages on Linux-based industrial PCs (IPCs) and test systems&nbsp;
- Read stack traces, application logs, and system output to isolate where and why a failure occurred, and deliver actionable findings to developers&nbsp;
- Identify, thoroughly document, and track bugs in GitLab throughout the development cycle, with clear steps to reproduce and supporting logs or screenshots. Work with developers to verify fixes and confirm no regressions
- Use git and GitLab daily to check out branches and tags under test, review merge requests and pipelines to understand what changed, and manage issues and epics&nbsp;
Hardware and System Testing&nbsp;

- Perform hands-on testing of POR robotic systems, including InductOne, verifying that software, electrical, and mechanical sub-systems work together end to end&nbsp;
- Troubleshoot at the system level to determine whether a fault originates in software, electrical, or mechanical sub-systems&nbsp;
Collaboration and Leadership&nbsp;

- Be an advocate for our customers and end users by holding a high standard for quality and usability&nbsp;
- Work with product owners to confirm features meet requirements and intended customer use, and participate in acceptance and release sign-off&nbsp;
- Present QA data, test results, and analyses to stakeholders, including customers, leadership, and cross-functional teams, in a clear, accessible manner tailored to the audience&nbsp;&nbsp;
- Mentor interns and junior-level teammates by sharing QA best practices, providing technical guidance, reviewing their work, and supporting their professional development&nbsp;


Qualifications&nbsp;
Required&nbsp;

- Strong software QA fundamentals: test strategy, test plan development, test case design, bug reporting, regression testing, fix verification, and acceptance testing&nbsp;
- Proficient in Python, TypeScript, or a similar language used in test automation&nbsp;
- Working proficiency with the Linux command line, including file system navigation, permissions, SSH, managing services, and reading logs&nbsp;
- Experience installing and deploying software builds or deploy packages to test or production systems&nbsp;
- Experience with git and GitLab (or GitHub): branches, tags, merge requests, and issue tracking&nbsp;
- Experience testing hardware or physical systems, or a demonstrated aptitude and willingness to learn hands-on hardware testing&nbsp;
- Excellent verbal and written communication skills in English&nbsp;
- Ability to prioritize and manage multiple projects simultaneously in a dynamic environment&nbsp;
Preferred&nbsp;

- Experience with testing frameworks such as Pytest, Puppeteer, Playwright, or similar. Familiarity with C++
- Experience with CI/CD pipelines, ideally GitLab CI&nbsp;
- Experience with Docker or other containerized deployments&nbsp;


Required Education and Experience&nbsp;

- A bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Electrical&nbsp;or Mechanical Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent industry experience&nbsp;
- 5+ years of experience in QA or test engineering, with the majority in software testing&nbsp;
- 2+ years of hands-on experience developing software test automation&nbsp;
- Experience testing products that combine software and hardware, such as robotics, automation, or embedded systems&nbsp;


Work Environment &amp; Travel&nbsp;

- This position operates in a professional office setting with occasional exposure to robotic systems and moving mechanical parts. The noise level in the work environment and job sites may at times be loud.&nbsp;
- There is some travel expected for the purposes of customer support and deployments.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Position Type/Expected Hours of Work/Locatio
Full time, 40 hours/week between M-F, 9:00am-6:00pm, In office at our San Antonio based HQ.


Salary Information
The range for this role starts at $112,000 per year. Starting salary is based on years of experience.


We are not able to provide visa sponsorship for this role.

L3Harris is dedicated to recruiting and developing high-performing talent who are passionate about what they do. Our employees are unified in a shared dedication to our customers’ mission and quest for professional growth. L3Harris provides an inclusive, engaging environment designed to empower employees and promote work-life success. Fundamental to our culture is an unwavering focus on values, dedication to our communities, and commitment to excellence in everything we do.

L3Harris is the Trusted Disruptor in defense tech. With customers’ mission-critical needs always in mind, our employees deliver end-to-end technology solutions connecting the space, air, land, sea and cyber domains in the interest of national security.

Job Title: Sr. Associate, Software Quality Engineer 

Job Code: 46431

Job Location: Nashville, TN

Job Schedule: 9/80 employees work 9 out of 14 days- totaling 80 hours worked- and have every other Friday off

Role is contingent upon program award

Job Description:

The Software Quality Engineer is responsible for creating end-to-end test plans, executing the test plan, and managing all activities in the plan as part of and in conjunction with an Agile Scrum development team to ensure that all objectives are met and the software solution works as expected. The solution should be tested in terms of functionality, performance, stability, and compatibility with legacy and/or third party software and integrated external hardware.

The objective of the Software Quality Engineer is to ensure that testing of every feature of the software solution and through every phase of development is well defined, planned, and executed. The work of the Software Quality Engineer should inspire confidence that any potential issue has been identified and addressed prior to release of the software solution. The Software Quality Engineer, Senior Associate Level is a professional with job area knowledge and a key contributor to the scrum team.

Essential Functions:



- Review functional and design specifications to ensure full understanding of individual deliverables;
- Identify test requirements from Conditions of Acceptance, map test case requirements, and design test coverage plan;
- Develop, document and maintain functional test cases and other test artifacts such as test plans, test summaries, and process documents as needed;
- Execute and evaluate manual test cases and report test results;
- Participate in test case reviews with cross-functional team members;
- Identify any potential quality issues per defined process and escalate potential quality issues immediately to Product Owners;
- Keep team and stakeholders informed of project QA progress and emergent risks;
- Ensure that validated deliverables meet functional and design specifications and requirements via Functional, Regression, Performance, Stress, and Endurance Testing;
- Isolate, replicate, and report defects and verify defect fixes via Exploratory, and Usability Testing in addition to above testing methods;
- Seek opportunities for improvement in quality, including but not limited to efficiency gains and expanding test coverage;
- Engage as an active participant in Scrum ceremonies;
- Required to perform other appropriate duties as requested, directed, or assigned;
- Perform all job functions with a positive, professional attitude;
- Ability to obtain a US Secret security clearance 


Qualifications:



- Bachelor’s Degree and a minimum of 2 years of prior related experience. Graduate Degree or equivalent with 0 to 2 years of prior related experience. In lieu of a degree, minimum of 6 years of prior related experience. 


Preferred Additional Skills:



- Knowledge and experience in test design, development, and execution of test cases, in support of software and hardware solutions; 
- Excellent observational, analytical, and problem-solving skills;
- Excellent listening and interpersonal skills;
- Ability to stay disciplined and focused;
- Strong written and verbal communication skills;
- Able to be productive and effective working either alone or as part of a team;
- Strong customer service orientation;
- Experience working in a team-oriented, collaborative environment.
- Experience with Test Track Pro, Version One, or similar testing tools/suites;
- Experience with software that directly interfaces with 3rd party firmware;
- Experience in an Agile Scrum environment;
- Familiarity with closed network environments;
- US Government security clearance.




L3Harris Technologies is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. L3Harris is committed to treating all employees and applicants for employment with respect and dignity and maintaining a workplace that is free from unlawful discrimination. All applicants will be considered for employment without regard to race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, ethnicity, gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, breastfeeding or other related medical conditions), gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, marital status, veteran status, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, characteristic or membership in any other group protected by federal, state or local laws. L3Harris maintains a drug-free workplace and performs pre-employment substance abuse testing and background checks, where permitted by law.

Please be aware many of our positions require the ability to obtain a security clearance. Security clearances may only be granted to U.S. citizens. In addition, applicants who accept a conditional offer of employment may be subject to government security investigation(s) and must meet eligibility requirements for access to classified information.

